      "extract": "\\label{sec:definition} Let $M$ be a closed, orientable 3--manifold. A \\textbf{link} in $M$ is a (possibly empty, possibly disconnected) closed 1--submanifold $L$ of $M.$ We consider links up to (not necessarily orientation preserving) diffeomorphisms of their complement $M\\setminus L$. This is motivated by the fact that none of the invariants we consider in this article differ on non-isotopic links with",
