      "extract": "According to J\\o{}rgensen--Thurston theory \\cite{thurston-notes,Gro81, Mai10}, for each positive real number $v$, there are at most finitely many hyperbolic 3--manifolds of volume $v.$ We show that the analogous result holds for topological volume. \\begin{proposition}\\label{pro:finiteness} For each positive real number $v$, there are at most finitely many closed, orientable 3--manifolds of topological volume $v.$",
