      "extract": "\\label{sec:covers} It is straightforward to see that hyperbolic volume is multiplicative under finite-sheeted covers. The following example shows that the analogous fact is not true for topological volume in general. \\begin{example} We show in \\cref{sec:computations} that $m009$ (Snappy notation) is the unique minimiser of $\\R P^3,$ and hence $\\volt(\\R P^3)=\\volh(m009)\\approx 2.66674$. One sees this by noting that",
